menu "Wendy board benchmarks"
    config WENDY_KORVO_BENCHMARK
        bool "Run Korvo-1 memory and SIMD benchmarks at startup"
        default n
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31
        help
            Runs bounded memory-copy and INT8 convolution benchmarks on Core 1
            ten seconds after startup, then reports heap headroom every five
            seconds while camera/audio/networking run. Requires PSRAM and
            both CPU cores; configuration fails if either is disabled.
            Output lines contain
            WENDY_BENCH followed by JSON. The convolution output is compared
            with ESP-NN's ANSI reference implementation before timing it.

            Intended for hardware qualification, not release firmware. This
            temporarily competes with application tasks and uses ESP-NN's
            global convolution scratch buffer. Do not enable in a firmware
            that runs another ESP-NN convolution user concurrently.
endmenu
